<title>SINGAPORE: India sells Dec low sulphur fuel oil to BP.</title>
<headline>India sells Dec low sulphur fuel oil to BP.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has awarded a tender to sell 20,000 tonnes of low sulphur residue fuel oil to British Petroleum &amp; Co Plc, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>Traders said BP bought the cargo at &quot;a very high price&quot; but both IOC and BP declined to comment on the price.</p>
<p>The tender, which closed November 21, sought to sell a cargo of 75-centistoke fuel oil of 1.2 percent sulphur heavy residue for lifting from Vizag between December 1-3.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65-870-3082).</p>
